2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2372) 'Heavy compute runs in a godot-sandbox guest, never as a host pipeline or a GDScript loop.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2372) 'A native ggml engine module, a GDExtension ggml API and a standalone runtime are all off the route.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2372) 'Check a new heavy compute job against the rule: put it in a riscv64 guest ELF or on ggml-rd with compute-rd.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2372) 'heavy compute runs in a godot-sandbox guest
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2372) '- Heavy compute runs in a godot-sandbox guest: a riscv64 guest ELF on the CPU, which is also the parity oracle, or kernels on ggml-rd with compute-rd, authored in Lean and lowered through Slang to SPIR-V (RFD66606-2265).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2372) '- It never runs as a host Python or C++ pipeline or as a GDScript loop.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2372) '- ggml runs only in such a guest (RFD66606-2290).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2372) '- RFD66606-2294, where this rule lived before the split.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2372  1 LINE
 Text:Written

